# IRC from the 21-atom (complete ester bridge) TS.
#
# Purpose: show what the single imaginary mode at -490.3 cm-1 actually connects.
# The mode moved from -313 (17-atom QM region) to -490 (21-atom), and the TS
# geometry moved with it (C128-O133 1.730 -> 1.607 A), so the mode tally alone
# cannot say whether this is the same saddle. The IRC decides.
#
# Geometry: ../optts_bridge/job.xyz (full-system B97-3c TightOpt TS, QM1 = 21
# atoms).
#
# Same method/solvent as the geometry+freq tier (the manual requires it for an
# IRC). InitHess left at ORCA's default: a standalone IRC computes a fresh
# numerical Hessian at the start, which is what we want. MaxIter raised from the
# 20 that the r2SCAN-3c IRC hit in BOTH directions without reaching a minimum.
#
# Monitors are 0-based: C128-O133 the forming bond, C128=O129 the carbonyl,
# O133-O134 the peroxide, O133-H132 the transferring proton.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) IRC TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132 133 134 135 136}
END
Charge_total 0
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%irc
  MaxIter 50
  Direction both
  Monitor_Internals
    {B 128 133}
    {B 129 128}
    {B 133 132}
  end
END

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile 0 1 job.xyz
